{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The refactor is structurally valid; both failures occur because `HomBisimilarity.refl` expects the state as an explicit argument. Applying it to `s'` supplies the required `s' ~[lts] s'` witness while preserving the reduced direct use of `follow_fst` and `follow_snd`.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro h\\n  use @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs, ChoiceBisim.choice h\\n  intro s₁ s₂ hs μ\\n  cases hs with\\n  | choice h =>\\n    constructor\\n    · intro s' ht\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨q', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n        exact ⟨q', Tr.choiceL ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        exact ⟨s', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim (HomBisimilarity.refl s')⟩\\n    · intro s' ht\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨p', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n        exact ⟨p', Tr.choiceL ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        exact ⟨s', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim (HomBisimilarity.refl s')⟩\\n  | bisim h =>\\n    constructor\\n    · intro s' ht\\n      obtain ⟨q', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n      exact ⟨q', ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n    · intro s' ht\\n      obtain ⟨p', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n      exact ⟨p', ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\"}"}}
